                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">59e0b89a-e487-49f8-bab8-b5bab16be14c</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">d3252b1e-bd6b-43f0-b571-6bf993cf5578</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10"></item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">NATURAL VENTILATION
The one path that joins an OUTDOOR wind result
to an INDOOR one. Units: METERS.

CHAIN (bottom row, left to right):
Facade Wind Pressure (EN 1991-1-4)
  -&gt; Mean Wind Vm at the opening height
Window Air Exchange (Maas 1995)
  -&gt; Flow m3/h through the open window
Division by 3600 (and by the 1 m2 opening)
  -&gt; Indoor Inlet Speed in m/s
Indoor Case -&gt; Run

FACADE WIND PRESSURE: basic wind 25 m/s, opening
at z = 5 m, building 10 x 10 m, opening 1.5 m2,
zone D (windward), terrain 3 (suburban) - all
component defaults.

WINDOW AIR EXCHANGE, from the Maas 1995 unit
test: opening 1 m2, sash 1.5 m, dT 10 K, room
volume 50 m3, 0.0043 L/s per occupant, 1
occupant. The test's hand-evaluated case is the
same numbers at 3 m/s wind:
  Q = 1800 * sqrt(0.1179) m3/h.
Disconnect the Vm wire and type 3 into Wind Speed
to reproduce it exactly.

ROOM 5 x 4 x 2.5 m = 50 m3, matching the pinned
Room Volume. Window 1 m2 on x=0, same-size
opening on x=5 for cross ventilation. Cell size
0.25 m is the Indoor Case default - no fixture
pins a cell size for this workflow.

Action toggles ship OFF.</item>
                  </items>
